  "question": {
    "text": "The block shown in the diagram has a mass of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>μg</mi></math> and a charge of <math><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mo>×</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>–</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>. If the block is given an initial velocity of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> in the x-direction&nbsp;at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;and an electric field of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;is switched on in the x-direction, then the range (&nbsp;<math><mtext>R</mtext></math>&nbsp;) of the block on the ground will be<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/ci/image164-65323afc-731e-4fdf-9229-31a71dec7258.jpg\" style=\"height: 134px; width: 240px;\" />",
